x86_64: stack struct arguments at their own width, odd sizes repaired

Upstream: cisco/ChezScheme#1091, merged 2026-11-05. This is that PR's two
x86_64 commits on cisco/ChezScheme main,
251d3962b42b4f33e7dcbb6be023f4f99da78c24 (store a stack struct's sub-word
pieces at their own width) and 048879e36460dc831a4737a2f5967fc3d34f42e1
(foreign call and callable repairs for odd-sized struct arguments), and
applied to v10.4.1 it makes the same change line for line. No Chez release
has them yet (the newest is v10.4.1), so jolt carries them until the first
one that does. Delete this file in the change that moves jolt to that
release; test/chez/ffi-stack-args-test.ss checks the placement either way.

diff --git a/s/x86_64.ss b/s/x86_64.ss
index 93225b8..78a0674 100644
--- a/s/x86_64.ss
+++ b/s/x86_64.ss
